**1. An electromagnetic valve actuator comprising:**

a magnetic core movable between a first position and a second position to actuate a valve;

an electric coil configured, when energized, to generate a magnetic field that moves the magnetic core;

a current-sensing circuit configured to generate a signal indicative of current flowing through the electric coil; and

a controller operatively coupled to the electric coil and the current-sensing circuit, the controller configured to:

select a time interval associated with energization of the electric coil;

determine, from the signal, a change in the current flowing through the electric coil during the selected time interval;

evaluate the change against at least one error criterion; and

generate an actuator-error indication in response to the change satisfying the at least one error criterion.

1. A valve system comprising:  
a valve body defining a fluid passage;  
a valve member movable between a first position and a second position to control fluid flow through the fluid passage;  
a solenoid including a coil configured, when energized, to move the valve member;  
a current-sensing circuit configured to generate coil-current data indicative of electrical current through the coil; and  
a fault-detection controller configured to determine, from the coil-current data, a temporal coil-current evaluation product representing a relationship between the electrical current through the coil and an elapsed energization time, compare the temporal coil-current evaluation product with a predefined limit, and generate a fault indication in response to the temporal coil-current evaluation product satisfying a fault criterion relative to the predefined limit.

### Exemplary Apparatus Claim

1. **An electromagnetic actuator system comprising:**

   an electromagnetic actuator including a coil and a core movable relative to the coil in response to energization of the coil;

   a current sensing circuit configured to generate a current signal representative of an electrical current flowing through the coil; and

   a controller operatively coupled to the coil and the current sensing circuit, the controller being configured to:

   identify a time section during which the coil is energized;

   determine a start-current value representing the electrical current at a beginning of the time section;

   determine an end-current value representing the electrical current at an end of the time section;

   determine a duration of the time section; and

   detect an error condition of the electromagnetic actuator based on the start-current value, the end-current value, and the duration.

2. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to calculate a current-change parameter from a difference between the end-current value and the start-current value.

3. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 2**, wherein the current-change parameter comprises a rate of current change determined by dividing the difference by the duration.

4. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 2**, wherein the controller is configured to detect the error condition by comparing the current-change parameter with at least one predetermined threshold or expected value.

5. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1**, wherein the error condition indicates at least one of incomplete movement of the core, impeded movement of the core, failure of the core to move, an electrical fault of the coil, or an abnormal actuator operating state.

6. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to define the beginning and the end of the time section relative to application of an actuation voltage to the coil.

7. **The electromagnetic actuator system of claim 1**, wherein the controller is further configured to generate an error signal, inhibit further energization of the coil, or store diagnostic information in response to detecting the error condition.

### Exemplary Method Claim

8. **A method for monitoring an electromagnetic actuator having a coil and a core movable relative to the coil, the method comprising:**

   energizing the coil to cause movement of the core;

   monitoring an electrical current flowing through the coil over a time section;

   determining a start-current value at a beginning of the time section;

   determining an end-current value at an end of the time section;

   determining a duration of the time section; and

   detecting an error condition of the electromagnetic actuator using the start-current value, the end-current value, and the duration.

9. **The method of claim 8**, further comprising calculating a rate-of-change value according to a difference between the end-current value and the start-current value divided by the duration, wherein detecting the error condition comprises comparing the rate-of-change value with a reference criterion.

10. **The method of claim 8**, wherein detecting the error condition comprises evaluating whether a current profile associated with movement of the core deviates from an expected current profile.
